|desc=
When casting damaging spells or mind attacks, the release of your willpower can call forth a meteor to crash down near your foes.

The meteor deals {{fire}} and {{physical}} damage in radius 2, each equal to 25 + 2.5 × the higher of your Spellpower and Mindpower, and stuns enemies for 3 turns.

Lava is created in radius 3 around the impact dealing {{fire}} damage per turn for 8 turns, equal to 30 + the higher of your Spellpower and Mindpower. This will overwrite tiles that already have modified terrain.

You and your allies take no damage from either effect.

Additionally, your {{fire}} damage bonus and resistance penetration is set to your current highest damage bonus and resistance penetration. This applies to all {{fire}} damage you deal.

The damage scales with your Spellpower or Mindpower.
}}
===Notes===
*The meteor can trigger at most once per turn, and only when your spell or mind power actually damages a creature. It lands on that creature's tile.
*Damage and stun chance use whichever of Spellpower and Mindpower is higher. Both the meteor and the lava can critically hit.
*Only the center tile of the impact is always turned to lava. Every other tile in radius 3 has a 40% chance.
*The description is wrong about modified terrain. The lava can't replace terrain that is already changed by another temporary effect. This includes:
**Lava from any meteor, including {{t|Meteor Slam}} and {{t|Anomaly Meteor}}
**Lava from volcano effects such as {{t|Erupting Darkness}} and {{t|Seismic Activity}}
**Summoned walls such as {{t|Stone Wall}}, {{t|Ice Wall}} or {{t|Materialize Barrier}}
**Other temporary ground such as {{t|Jumpgate}} or {{t|Forge Bellows}}
*{{t|Meteor Slam}} and {{t|Rain of Fire}} require [[Ashes of Urh'Rok]].